  "TITLE": "The Habit Loop:<br>Why Procedures Become<br>Automatic (or Don't)",
  "LEAD": "A habit is a closed loop &mdash; a cue triggers a routine, the routine delivers a reward, and the reward strengthens the link between that cue and that routine, so next time the cue alone is enough to trigger it. Repeat the loop enough times and control shifts from the deliberate, effortful prefrontal cortex to the fast, automatic basal ganglia &mdash; the same behavior needs less and less conscious attention to fire.",
